<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43152" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sculptūra</span></b> , ae, f.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				cutting out</i>, <i>carving in relief</i>, <i>sculpture</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">anulus, cujus gemmae sculptura erat Proserpinae
					raptus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Ner. 46</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">anulus ejusdem sculpturae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Just.
					15, 4, 5</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Quint. 2, 21,
			9</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			Concr., esp. in plur., <i>marbles</i>, <i>works of plastic art</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 16,
				40, 77, § 209</span></i> (Jahn, scalptura); <i><span class="en">Vitr. 2,
			9</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
